today there was a very large transaction  16 06 bitcoin worth about 1 billion was  moved for a transaction fee of a dollar  and 75 cents across the bitcoin network  think about that for a second somebody  moved one billion dollars of bitcoin  across the bitcoin blockchain and they  paid 1.75  the legacy system literally would think  that's egregious every single middleman  every single rent seeker would want  their hands in the pot if somebody was  going to go move a billion dollars the  bankers would want a little bit the  financial advisors would want a little  bit the platforms would run a little bit  the wire services would want a little  bit everybody would want to get paid you  want to move a billion dollars well you  got to pay us to do it the bitcoin  blockchain doesn't care it literally is  going to destroy those middlemen those  rent seekers and so to move one billion  dollars for a transaction fee of 1.75 is  pretty damn cool this is as bitcoin  magazine said here the magic of bitcoin  so to continue to see things like this i  think reiterate to people this is not  just about an asset it is not only about  having a finite supply in a world where  there's undisciplined monetary and  fiscal policy this is a technology  platform it is a payment rail it is  superior technology it is a  decentralized distributed network that  allows for peer-to-peer transactions  without asking for permission from  anyone and when you start to evaluate  the software based on merit you realize  that no one can compete with it where  else in the world  can you send 1 billion dollars for a  dollar 75 without needing any sort of  middleman and being able to do it faster  than any other service this is what  bitcoin can do and so ultimately i think  what we're watching here is that a lot  of folks are going to start opening  their eyes they're not only looking at  the asset they're also going to start to  evaluate what that payment rail looks  like and as we've seen whether it's  twitter integrating strike or we've seen  the lightning network continue to grow  in popularity or things like this where  somebody moves that billion dollars for  a dollar seventy five  over time there's familiarity there's  education and we start to get some sort  of adoption that looks like mainstream  adoption it's not enough to simply just  have bitcoins it's not enough to simply  just have the first movers instead what  we need is we need to have that  mainstream adoption if we then go and we  look well what is actually happening in  the market we can see that the bitcoin  supply on exchanges at the lowest level  it has been since 2018. now if you think  about bitcoin exchange supply one of the  key things here is that the bitcoin  supply on the exchange is a signal that  people could be ready to sell the  bitcoin if i'm buying bitcoin i'm going  to hold it for a long time i'm going to  go on an exchange i'm going to convert  dollars a stable coin or some other  asset into bitcoin and then i'm going to  withdraw the bitcoin into my own self  custody or my own cold storage and so  taking it off of the exchange is usually  a signal for long-term holders and so  the more bitcoin that's on exchanges the  more likely there is to be cell pressure  with the click of a button i can go  ahead and i can sell my bitcoin into the  market but if i actually go and i buy  bitcoin and i take it off the exchange  i'm adding friction to the ability to  sell it in the future because i have to  put it back on the exchange in order to  sell it but also what i am doing is i am  signaling that i plan to hold it for a  long period of time and so 2018 was the  bottom of the bear market of course  there was tons of bitcoin on the  exchanges at the bottom of 2018 because  we had seen a ton of cell pressure  everyone was ready to sell bitcoin now  all of a sudden as we get into the  higher ends of a bull market  what we can see is that people are not  ready to sell we are at the lowest level  of bitcoin on exchanges since 2018. and  so that is that signal that people are  buying it they're going to hold it and  they do not plan to sell it in the  future we know that about 85 percent of  the supply has not been sold in the last  90 days or so  and that usually leads to that supply  shock thesis we saw in october of 2020  when we had about 85 percent of the  supply not being sold for months on end  all of a sudden demand increases from  institutions we saw a lot of people  arbiting that greyscale gbtc fund all  those inflows led to a massive price  appreciation over 600 percent leading  into q1 of 2021. as we sit here today we  can see that not only is there very few  bitcoin that are actually on the  exchanges we also know that a lot of the  bitcoin that is being held has not moved  as well in the last few months and then  when you overlay that with the bitcoin  etfs and also things around interactive  brokers now letting ras come to the  market and also players like pimco who  have trillions of dollars all saying hey  we want to play in this game that  signals that there's going to be  increased demand there's a highly  illiquid supply and if history is any  guide that should lead to a massive  price appreciation in the coming months  it will be very interesting to watch now  one of the things that is going to start  to happen as the price of bitcoin  continues to go up is that people will  stop talking about bitcoin necessarily  it won't just be about oh that costs  three bitcoin today three bitcoin ends  up being about 180 000 you don't just go  to the store and spend 180 000 out of  the blue so we can't keep talking about  bitcoin at some point we're going to  have to start talking about sats or  satoshi's and those sets end up being  really hard to actually write out if  we're going to use eight decimal places  and so when you start to actually think  about a sat you can say one sat equals  how many dollars or you can give one  dollar equals how many sats and so today  what we've seen is that one dollar  equals about  1580 sats the ultimate idea from most  hardcore bitcoiners is that eventually  one dollar will equal one sat  as we've seen we continue to see that  one dollar equivalent in satoshi's goes  down we're moving from at one point we  were at 10 million satoshi's equaled one  dollar then we were down at a million  then at 100k then we were at 10k then we  were at 1.6 k and now we were at just  under at  1580 satoshi's so over time it is likely  that the amount of satoshi's it will  take to purchase one dollar is going to  continue to trend towards one and if we  eventually reach dollar parity where one  dollar equals one sat bitcoin will be at  a much higher price obviously and so as  we watch this occur it's important to  remember that as the price of bitcoin  goes up people will come in they will  not be able to actually purchase one  full bitcoin today it costs 60 000  that is more than a large portion of the  american population makes in a single  year on top of that what we have to  remind them is not only can they buy a  fraction of a bitcoin but they can also  spend a fraction of a bitcoin they can  spend satoshi's and if we begin to  educate people on the fractional  ownership of this asset and the ability  to spend those fractions of a bitcoin my  guess is that we will slowly start to  see a repricing of assets both of goods  and services in satoshis it is very  unlikely that somebody is going to say  hey you can come here and you can  actually purchase this  piece of uh this good from the grocery  store or this service and it's going to  cost you 0.0001 bitcoin no instead they  would just list it in satoshi's and so  that ends up being the next big phase  here we already have the mainstream  adoption of individuals we now are in  the institutional adoption phase where  financial institutions and corporations  are all jumping in that institutional  cohort really important we then are just  on the precipice of seeing the  nation-states start to adopt this  whether it's sovereign wealth funds  which we've heard anthony scaramucci and  kevin o'leary talk about the last few  days or it's nation-states like el  salvador maybe even rumors around brazil  or others starting to actually buy the  asset hold the asset or give the asset  to their citizens but on top of all of  that the next big phase is after the  adoption  we will start to start pricing goods and  services in satoshis and so be very  interesting to see this because on the  internet rather than have individual  geographic based assets my guess is that  we will start to see more and more  pricing in satoshis and lastly is don't  forget that this has been a long journey  this journey has been going on for  literally more than a decade it is not  something that just popped up in 2017 or  2018. if we go all the way back just to  2013 you know about four years after  bitcoin actually was launched you can  see here that the money magazine said  that the winklevoss's idea around a  bitcoin etf was number five on the 20  dumbest things of 2013. number five 20  dumbest things of 2013. well the  winklevosses they got the last laugh  they made the infamous purchase of 210  000 bitcoin right around that time seems  to have turned out pretty well for them  they're both multi-billionaires but on  top of that eric voorhees calling out  that anyone who sold their car for 10  000 and bought bitcoin upon seeing this  now has three million dollars so you  could have said in 2013 this sounds like  a dumb idea but now here we are we have  multiple etfs trading in the market in  the united states and many more abroad  and so maybe it wasn't a dumb idea maybe  it's just that the world didn't actually  understand what they were watching occur  and the winklevosses did so what do we  think in terms of uh kind of where we  are and how long this has been  building up to but it feels like now  we're at a point where it's 